  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A heavy iron bar of weight <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is having its one end on the ground and the other on the shoulder of a man. The rod makes an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with the horizontal, the normal force applied by the man on bar is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>wt</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>wt</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>wt</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>wt</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let's consider the following diagram:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0065_6c8566f6cba0.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 235px;\"/></p><p>For the equilibrium of the system, the net torque, according to the above figure, on the system about point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> should be zero.</p><p>With reference to the above figure, the net anti-clockwise torque about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>L</mi><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And, the net clockwise torque about the same point is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Equations (1) and (2) imply that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>L</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>×</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mi>L</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the required weight can be expressed as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>wt</mi></math></p>"
  }
}